From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:32:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] output-management: A resize keeps the output where it is

A viewer that asks for another size sends a layout that starts at 0,0.
wayvnc passed that position on, so the resized headless output landed on
top of the compositor's other outputs: clicks went to the wrong screen
and the windows of both overlapped. Only the size and the transform
are the viewer's to choose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/output-management.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/output-management.c b/src/output-management.c
index a70934c..092f330 100644
--- a/src/output-management.c
+++ b/src/output-management.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ struct output_manager_head {
 	struct wl_list modes;
 	char* name;
 	bool enabled;
+	int32_t x, y;
 };
 
 static struct wl_list heads;
@@ -101,6 +102,9 @@ static void output_head_position(void* data,
 		struct zwlr_output_head_v1* output_head, int32_t x, int32_t y)
 {
 	nvnc_trace("Got head position: %d,%d", x, y);
+	struct output_manager_head* head = data;
+	head->x = x;
+	head->y = y;
 }
 
 static void output_head_transform(void* data,
@@ -346,8 +350,13 @@ bool wlr_output_manager_configure_output(
 		zwlr_output_configuration_head_v1_set_custom_mode(
 			config_head, width, height, refresh_rate);
 
+		/* The viewer's layout starts at 0,0 and knows nothing of the
+		 * compositor's other outputs: with x and y the output would
+		 * land on top of them. Where it is stays the compositor's
+		 * business.
+		 */
 		zwlr_output_configuration_head_v1_set_position(config_head,
-				x, y);
+				head->x, head->y);
 
 		/* It doesn't make any sense to have rotation on a
 		 * headless display, so we set the transform here to be
-- 
